+## Whole-line replacements (v8)
+
+Guarded edits use `replacement_mode: "lines"` by default. Replacement lines adopt
+the last applicable LF/CRLF ending at the original range. A nonempty replacement
+without a final newline retains the replaced range's original terminator, including
+at EOF. An originally unterminated EOF stays unterminated unless the supplied
+replacement explicitly adds a newline. Empty text deletes the entire range.
+Use `replacement_mode: "exact"` to copy replacement bytes verbatim, intentionally
+join lines, remove an EOF terminator or change line-ending style. LSP plans retain
+the server's exact edits and do not pass through this line normalization.
